    "body": "@tkent-google @rniwa @hober since you all were involved in the discussion of the formdata event, I thought it'd be worth tagging you for thoughts on this. It seems like a pretty reasonable feature request to me that would make form validation more useful.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, I wonder about whether this is a pattern we want to encourage. Since the server has to validate anyway, this effectively means making the user wait twice for server-side validation---once on the client-side, and once on the server-side. It could lead to weird experiences, too, where sometimes the client-side catches an error, but sometimes the server-side, so users wouldn't be sure what kind of validation experience they'd be getting. Currently there's a pretty clear division where client-side is used for quick synchronous checks on the \"form\" of the input, and the server side is used for more serious \"business logic\" checks.\r\n\r\nHmm.",
