    "updated_at": "2018-04-30T12:36:01Z",
    "body": "> I wonder about whether this is a pattern we want to encourage. Since the server has to validate anyway, this effectively means making the user wait twice for server-side validation\r\n\r\nOn the contrary they need to wait for many other request (images, css & js) when following that action to just to see a error on the same page making it as a simple reload of the hole page. and in worse case having to fill in some fields once more like a captcha image or password field where some backends are not as good at preserving the state.",
